          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A group of Year 7 students was polled on their favourite foods.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If 40 students participated in the survey, find how many of them chose:",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p35-q7-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"source page 35 p35-q7-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm,every node/.style={font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black,inner sep=0pt,outer sep=0pt}]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\coordinate (C) at (0,0);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (C) circle[radius=30];\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (90:30)--(C)--(270:30);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.8pt] (180:30)--(C)--(216:30);\n\\node at (0:15) {chocolate};\n\\node at (135:17) {chips};\n\\node at (198:21) {pies};\n\\node at (243:20) {fruit};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
        "widthMm": 62,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
        "axes": null,
        "spec": {
          "sourcePage": 35,
          "sourceRegion": "Question 7, graph to the right of parts a–d",
          "description": "Directly labelled sector graph. Chocolate occupies the right semicircle, chips the upper-left quarter, pies the smaller lower-left sector adjoining the horizontal radius, and fruit the remaining lower-left sector. No numerical annotations, centre marker, right-angle marker or legend.",
          "mathematics": "Chocolate is one-half and chips one-quarter. The diagonal reconstruction radius at 216 degrees preserves the approximate source appearance: pies about 10% and fruit about 15%. This coordinate is an authoring value, not a supplied angle or exact student given.",
          "answerVisibility": "Only the original category labels and sector boundaries are visible. Frequencies, proportions and change calculations belong exclusively to answers."
        },
        "derived": false,
        "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
      }
    ],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p35-q7-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Chocolate",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$20$ students",
          "worked": "Chocolate occupies half the circle.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Chocolate students}&=\\frac12\\times40\\\\\\text{Chocolate students}&=20\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 9
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q7-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Fruit",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Approximately $6$ students",
          "worked": "The fruit sector represents approximately $15\\%$ of the circle.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Fruit students}&\\approx\\frac{15}{100}\\times40\\\\\\text{Fruit students}&\\approx6\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 9
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q7-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Chips",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$10$ students",
          "worked": "Chips occupies one-quarter of the circle.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Chips students}&=\\frac14\\times40\\\\\\text{Chips students}&=10\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 9
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q7-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Pies",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Approximately $4$ students",
          "worked": "The pies sector represents approximately $10\\%$ of the circle.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Pies students}&\\approx\\frac{10}{100}\\times40\\\\\\text{Pies students}&\\approx4\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 9
      },
      {
        "id": "p35-q7-e",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p35-q7-e-stem",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Another 20 students were surveyed.",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "break"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "10 chose chocolate and 10 chose chips.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p35-q7-e-i",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "Will the chips sector become larger or smaller? Explain your reasoning.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "Larger: $\\frac{20}{60}=\\frac13>\\frac14$.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{New total}&=40+20\\\\\\text{New total}&=60\\\\\\text{New chips count}&=10+10\\\\\\text{New chips count}&=20\\\\\\text{New chips share}&=\\frac{20}{60}\\\\\\text{New chips share}&=\\frac13\\end{align*}$$\nSince $\\frac13>\\frac14$, the chips sector becomes larger.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 20
          },
          {
            "id": "p35-q7-e-ii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "Will the chocolate sector become larger, smaller or stay the same size? Explain your reasoning.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "It stays the same size: $\\frac{30}{60}=\\frac12$.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Original chocolate share}&=\\frac{20}{40}\\\\\\text{Original chocolate share}&=\\frac12\\\\\\text{New chocolate share}&=\\frac{20+10}{40+20}\\\\\\text{New chocolate share}&=\\frac{30}{60}\\\\\\text{New chocolate share}&=\\frac12\\end{align*}$$\nThe proportion is unchanged, so the chocolate sector stays the same size.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 20
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
